# sirna-reproduction (Martinelli, bioRxiv 10.1101/2023.08.16.553554) supplementary
# training data (907 siRNAs, siRNAmod-derived): NOT integrated into the loader
# -- no gene/target-identity column (same disqualifier as Shmushkovich 2018),
# only sequence + chemical modification + PCT + a source PMID/patent-ID that
# would require per-document tracing (30 documents, one patent = 60% of rows)
# to recover gene identity. Kept locally for reference, never committed.
# See data/POTENTIAL_DATA_SOURCES.md / data/DATA_SOURCE_LEDGER.md.
data/raw/sirna_reproduction_martinelli_907.csv

# REMOVED REMOVED panel: the source repo ships no LICENSE file, so it is
# all-rights-reserved by default under GitHub's terms. Kept locally so the
# loader still works from a local checkout, never committed -- NOTICE.md and
# data/DATA_SOURCES.md have always described it this way, it was just tracked
# by mistake until now. It has no `sirna-data-fetch` fetcher, so a fresh clone
# cannot reproduce the subset; load_records() simply returns 8 fewer records.
data/raw/REMOVED

